    <!-- Origin story -->
    <section id="pq-origin-section" class="pq-section pq-origin">
      <div class="pq-origin-grid">
        <div class="pq-origin-text">
          <h2>The idea</h2>
          <p>
            Every summer growing up, my family and I road-tripped to national parks across the
            country. That's where I fell in love with them &mdash; how different one park could feel
            from the next, and how much of that variety is actually protected. I was crossing new
            parks off my list every summer, hoping to see them all someday.
          </p>
          <p>
            To celebrate graduating college, two childhood buddies and I planned something ambitious:
            drive over 3,000 miles, camp along the way, and visit every national park in California
            &mdash; which, with nine, has more national parks than any other state. In the months
            between graduation and the trip, I built ParkQuest, so we'd have a real way to log where
            we'd been and see what other people had found worth stopping for.
          </p>
          <p>
            It's grown into a personal journal for anyone chasing the same goal. Track your own
            visits, see what other adventurers found worth the stop, and work through the full list of
            63. And as a bonus, collect digital stamps and badges along the way.
          </p>
        </div>
